; jobarm.g -- the PERMISSION for ONE launch of a job file generated by the Workbench: a laser cut (Simple cuts) or a CNC file (CNC toolpaths).
; The Start of the page (CUT, or Start in CNC toolpaths) calls it right before it sends M32, once its own checks passed (machine free,
; mode, file made from the current design, work area and clamps, safety list). The first line of the generated file asks for this
; permission and uses it up: cutguard.g (laser cut) takes the Laser one, cncguard.g (CNC) the CNC one. A file of the page that is
; launched some other way (DWC Files, Jobs, the Send of Simulate job, a second M32) finds none and aborts before the laser or the
; spindle starts.
;
; Use:  M98 P"0:/sys/workshop/macros/guard/jobarm.g" A1 K"Laser"     arm: the next cutguard.g within 30 s lets that job go
;       M98 P"0:/sys/workshop/macros/guard/jobarm.g" A1 K"CNC"       arm: the next cncguard.g within 30 s lets that job go
;       M98 P"0:/sys/workshop/macros/guard/jobarm.g" A0              disarm both (the page does it when its start did not go through)
; (K = the kind of job, "Laser" or "CNC"; never P for a value: in M98 the P is the file name.)
;
; global.workshopLaserArmed / global.workshopCncArmed = the uptime second (state.upTime) until which the permission of that kind lasts;
; 0 = not armed. Each one is cleared by its guard when the job starts, by A0, by its own expiry and by a restart of the board. It is a
; guard against a launch by mistake, not a lock against someone who runs this macro by hand.

if !exists(param.A)
    abort "jobarm.g: A missing (1 = arm, 0 = disarm)"
if !exists(global.workshopCncArmed)
    global workshopCncArmed = 0
if !exists(global.workshopLaserArmed)
    global workshopLaserArmed = 0
if param.A == 1
    if !exists(param.K)
        abort "jobarm.g: K missing (Laser or CNC)"
    elif param.K == "Laser"
        set global.workshopLaserArmed = state.upTime + 30
    elif param.K == "CNC"
        set global.workshopCncArmed = state.upTime + 30
    else
        abort "jobarm.g: K must be Laser or CNC"
else
    set global.workshopLaserArmed = 0
    set global.workshopCncArmed = 0
